  {
    "id": "e38237ea5ae2f46a64559ff1",
    "path": "datafusion_session::table::ScanArgs::with_statistics_requests",
    "name": "with_statistics_requests",
    "owner": "datafusion_session::table::ScanArgs",
    "crate": "datafusion-session",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn with_statistics_requests(self, statistics_requests: &'a [StatisticsRequest]) -> Self",
    "docs": "Specifies the statistics the caller may use when optimizing the query.\n\nThis is intended to allow the `TableProvider` to cheaply provide\nstatistics that may help, such as those it has in an in-memory catalog\nor from some other metadata source.\n\n`TableProvider`s read these via [`Self::statistics_requests()`]; anything\na `TableProvider` cannot answer cheaply it simply ignores. DataFusion's\nown `TableProvider`s ignore this field — it exists so a request can be\nthreaded from a custom optimizer rule (which annotates\n`TableScan::statistics_requests`) through to a custom `TableProvider`.",
